      "message": "\u003e  (31 and no extensions) Toggle -\u003e Feature\n\nI don\u0027t think this can change physical device creation at[1] triggered at listing available system adapters?\n\n\nI think now I have an idea, what we want is this flag `--use-angle\u003ddesktop-min-version`, which makes a difference when initializing physical device\n\nExample log output difference with/without `--use-angle\u003ddesktop`\n```\n$ dawn_end2end_tests --backend\u003dopengles\n...\nSystem adapters: \n...\n - \"ANGLE (Google, Vulkan 1.3.0 (SwiftShader Device (Subzero) (0x0000C0DE)), SwiftShader driver-5.0.0)\" - \"OpenGL version OpenGL ES 3.1.0 (ANGLE 2.1.24454 git hash: 0bb109aa3311) [Selected]\"\n   type: CPU, backend: OpenGLES, compatibilityMode: true\n   vendorId: 0x0000, deviceId: 0xC0DE\n\n```\n\n```\n$ dawn_end2end_tests --backend\u003dopengles --use-angle\u003ddesktop\n...\nSystem adapters: \n...\n - \"ANGLE (NVIDIA Corporation, Quadro P1000/PCIe/SSE2, OpenGL 4.5.0 NVIDIA 535.183.06)\" - \"OpenGL version OpenGL ES 3.1.0 (ANGLE 2.1.24454 git hash: 0bb109aa3311) [Selected]\"\n   type: Unknown, backend: OpenGLES, compatibilityMode: true\n   vendorId: 0x10DE, deviceId: 0x0000\n   vendorName: nvidia, architecture:\n\n```",
