      "writtenOn": "2024-12-11T01:16:31Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "(if relevant after the other comments)\n\nThis is neat but I think it would be clearer to use a more common pattern, maybe:\n\n```cpp\n    auto default \u003d [\u0026](Toggle toggle, bool enabled) {\n        if (reinitialize) {\n            deviceToggles-\u003eDefaultOverride(toggle, enabled);\n        } else {\n            deviceToggles-\u003eDefault(toggle, enabled);\n        }\n    };\n```\n\nOr perhaps better, add a third argument like:\n```\nvoid TogglesState::Default(Toggle toggle, bool enabled,\n    TogglesState::Condition condition \u003d TogglesState::Condition::IfNotSet);\n```\nand here use:\n```\nauto cond \u003d reinitialize ?\n    TogglesState::Condition::IfNotForced :\n    TogglesState::Condition::IfNotSet;\ndeviceToggles-\u003eDefault(toggle, enabled, cond);\n```",
